# North Star

The North Star is **not** the planning chat, a status dashboard, or a dated
filename. It is two current files plus a versioned amendment log.

- `docs/north-star/CONSTITUTION.md` — purpose, **observable product outcome**,
  non-goals, invariants. Rare.
- `docs/north-star/LADDER.md` — the minimum path to that outcome. Changes more.
- `docs/north-star/AMENDMENTS/` — every pivot. Git history is not enough.

Always those paths. Never `NORTH_STAR_2026-07-30.md`. Status (shipped /
deployed / proven) lives in `WORKING_STATE.md` and gates, not the constitution.
Do not add a product `NORTH_STAR.md`.

## Always

- Session start: if those files are missing or still the stub, enter
  `/build-north-star` (staff the table, six lenses) and stay there (this pack
  repo is exempt). Refuse application code until the owner accepts v1.0.
- Ladder is the minimum risk-retiring path to the observable product outcome.
  Off-ladder work → `/amend-north-star`. A discovered risk is not a row.
- An invariant conflict → stop. Do not “interpret.” Propose an amendment.
- Implementation never edits constitution or ladder except by accepted amendment.

## Amendments

No silent drift. `/amend-north-star` first asks whether new evidence
threatens the observable product outcome, then the cheapest disposition.
Only builder-retired may add a row. Then six-lens injection. Bump the
in-file version. Leave the amendment record.
